`,e.jsxs(e.Fragment,{children:[e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["Phoenix provides support for retrieving and writing to Phoenix tables from within MapReduce jobs. The framework now provides custom ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"http://hadoop.apache.org/docs/current/api/org/apache/hadoop/mapreduce/InputFormat.html",children:"InputFormat"})," and ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"http://hadoop.apache.org/docs/current/api/org/apache/hadoop/mapreduce/OutputFormat.html",children:"OutputFormat"})," classes ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"https://github.com/apache/phoenix/blob/f84e5da33c21a728e73924c07506dd63e4621872/phoenix-core/src/main/java/org/apache/phoenix/mapreduce/PhoenixInputFormat.java",children:"PhoenixInputFormat"})," , ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"https://github.com/apache/phoenix/blob/f84e5da33c21a728e73924c07506dd63e4621872/phoenix-core/src/main/java/org/apache/phoenix/mapreduce/PhoenixOutputFormat.java",children:"PhoenixOutputFormat"}),"."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:[e.jsx(i.a,{href:"https://github.com/apache/phoenix/blob/f84e5da33c21a728e73924c07506dd63e4621872/phoenix-core/src/main/java/org/apache/phoenix/mapreduce/util/PhoenixMapReduceUtil.java",title:"PhoenixMapReduceUtil",children:"PhoenixMapReduceUtil"})," provides several utility methods to set the input and output configuration parameters to the job."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["When a Phoenix table is the source for the MapReduce job, we can provide a SELECT query or pass a table name and specific columns to import data. To retrieve data from the table within the mapper class, we need to have a class that implements ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"http://hadoop.apache.org/docs/current/api/org/apache/hadoop/mapred/lib/db/DBWritable.html",title:"DBWritable",children:"DBWritable"})," and pass it as an argument to ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"PhoenixMapReduceUtil.setInput"}),". The custom DBWritable class provides an implementation for ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"http://hadoop.apache.org/docs/current/api/org/apache/hadoop/mapreduce/lib/db/DBWritable.html#readFields%28java.sql.ResultSet%29",title:"readFields",children:"readFields(ResultSet rs)"})," that allows us to retrieve columns for each row. This custom DBWritable class will form the input value to the mapper class."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(i.blockquote,{children:[`
`,e.jsx(i.p,{children:"Note: The SELECT query must not perform any aggregation or use DISTINCT as these are not supported by our map-reduce integration."}),`
`]}),`
`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["Similarly, when writing to a Phoenix table, we use ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"PhoenixMapReduceUtil.setOutput"})," to set the output table and columns."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(i.blockquote,{children:[`
