`,e.jsxs(e.Fragment,{children:[e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["Phoenix uses Skip Scan for intra-row scanning which allows for ",e.jsx(i.a,{href:"/docs/fundamentals/performance#performance-skip-scan",children:"significant performance improvement"})," over Range Scan when rows are retrieved based on a given set of keys."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["Skip Scan leverages ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"SEEK_NEXT_USING_HINT"})," in HBase filters. It stores information about which key sets or key ranges are being searched for in each column. During filter evaluation, it checks whether a key is in one of the valid combinations or ranges. If not, it computes the next highest key to jump to."]}),`
`,e.jsxs(i.p,{children:["Input to ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"SkipScanFilter"})," is a ",e.jsx(i.code,{children:"List<List<KeyRange>>"})," where the top-level list represents each row-key column (that is, each primary key part), and the inner list represents OR-ed byte-array boundaries."]}),`
